Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||09-16-2001||12:18 AM||||When I am shifting from first to second or other gears, sometimes if the RPMs and the gears don't match, the car will jerk when the clutch is released.  Is this normal or am I supposed to rev the engine to its approximate RPMs for that gear?  Or I have a worn tranny?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Spektrum-87GT||09-16-2001||12:32 AM||||how long have you been driving a manual? that jerk usually happens if you let off the clutch too fast and dont give it enough gas. if you just started, it will come with experience.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||09-16-2001||12:35 AM||||Just as I thought.  I started recently.||||reg||1
Z||000003||formula2||09-16-2001||12:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>how long have you been driving a manual? that jerk usually happens if you let off the<BR>                    clutch too fast and dont give it enough gas. if you just started, it will come with<BR>                    experience.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I started recently too..But a new dog bone has helped me a lot..||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||09-16-2001||12:44 AM||||My GT was like that too. Turned out to be only me though. My 86SE V6 was an easy shifter but I found that I needed to feather the clutch and throttle just right for a nice smooth shift. I like the five speed, but I thought it was cool where Pontiac put reverse with the four speed. Passengers always get a kick out of watching you push down, pull towards you, and push forward for reverse. My 84 VW GTi was like that and I loved it.<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
